The '''2023–24 season''' was the 54th season in the history of [[Paris Saint-Germain F.C.|Paris Saint-Germain]] and its 50th consecutive season in the top flight. The club participated in [[2023–24 Ligue 1|Ligue 1]], the [[2023–24 Coupe de France|Coupe de France]], the [[2023–24 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]], and the [[2023 Trophée des Champions|Trophée des Champions]].

This was the first season since [[2016–17 Paris Saint-Germain F.C. season|2016–17]] without [[Neymar]] and [[Julian Draxler]], who both left the Parisian side to join Saudi Arabian club [[Al Hilal SFC|Al Hilal]] and the Qatari club [[Al Ahli SC (Doha)|Al Ahli]], and the first since [[2011–12 Paris Saint-Germain F.C. season|2011–12]] without [[Marco Verratti]], who joined Qatari club [[Al-Arabi SC (Qatar)|Al-Arabi]].

